What is printed by `p(3); q(3);` (spaces between digits only for readability)?

```c
#include <stdio.h>
void p(int n){ if (n == 0) return; printf("%d ", n); p(n-1); }
void q(int n){ if (n == 0) return; q(n-1); printf("%d ", n); }
int main(void){ p(3); q(3); return 0; }
```

What is printed?

```c
