```

`fib(0)=0`, `fib(1)=1`. The program below counts calls to `fib`. What is printed?

```c
#include <stdio.h>
int c = 0;
int fib(int n){ c++; if (n < 2) return n; return fib(n-1) + fib(n-2); }
int main(void){ fib(5); printf("%d", c); return 0; }
```

